{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966506-data-sphere-question","id":966506,"title":"Data Sphere Question","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-09T18:02:48-07:00","id":966506,"title":"Data Sphere Question","content":"Let's say I'm a Virtual Adept that's opted to use the Data Sphere in place of Correspondence.<br /> How exactly does range work now?<br /> <br /> If I had Data 3, does that mean I first need something of the targets like an old email account, and I'd have to roll Arete to generate 4 successes (taking an hour between rolls) before I can do any magic on them from a distance?<br /> Similarly, if I had Data 2 and I wanted to spy on someone, I'd need to have something fairly close to them like a current social media account before I could do the Arete rolls, get 6 (with two hours between rolls) before I can see them?<br /> <br /> Does having something closer to them make it any easier? Like if I had Data 4, would there be any difference at all if I had their Personal Email address instead of their IP address? Or does it take the same amount of time regardless?<br /> <br /> Also, how does this work for teleporting? Say I was on one side of a river and I wanted to teleport to the other side. Is this something Data allows or is this strictly a Correspondence thing? I know Teleporting is a thing with Data, but how does one establish a connection with their location?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T16:14:18-07:00","id":972189,"title":"","content":"Anyone at all?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T16:32:00-07:00","id":972195,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/828949-educate-me-on-the-data-sphere\">Here</a>'s the thread from when I was grappling with the Sphere.<br /> <br /> Data works by replacing the successes requirement for Correspondence ranges with a preliminary Intelligence + Enigmas action to get &quot;a bead&quot; on your target. More Data dots means that drawing a bead is easier, and that you can use a more tenuous link to draw a bead. During the process of drawing a bead, you require a connection at or below your level of Data. There's no clear duration on how long a &quot;lock&quot; lasts and how many effects you can cast with it, and there's no note as to how this affects the Arete roll, if at all, because Data seems somewhat sloppily conceived.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If I had Data 3, does that mean I first need something of the targets like an old email account, and I'd have to roll Arete to generate 4 successes (taking an hour between rolls) before I can do any magic on them from a distance? Similarly, if I had Data 2 and I wanted to spy on someone, I'd need to have something fairly close to them like a current social media account before I could do the Arete rolls, get 6 (with two hours between rolls) before I can see them? </div> </div> </div>The rolls are Int + Enigmas but otherwise, yes; you need a source of data to perform the Enigmas work to get a bead on your target, which takes some amount of time. This is before the Arete roll for the effect itself; you triangulate the target's location and then use Data 2 to scry, for instance.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Does having something closer to them make it any easier? Like if I had Data 4, would there be any difference at all if I had their Personal Email address instead of their IP address? Or does it take the same amount of time regardless? </div> </div> </div>The description <i>says </i>that skilled users find &quot;closer collections far easier to establish&quot; but the rules do not work this way. At Data 4, there's no difference between having their blood sample and having their IP address.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, how does this work for teleporting? Say I was on one side of a river and I wanted to teleport to the other side. Is this something Data allows or is this strictly a Correspondence thing? I know Teleporting is a thing with Data, but how does one establish a connection with their location? </div> </div> </div>Data can teleport. If you're teleporting LOS (other side of a street or river, assuming you can see across) then you don't need to use the Enigmas roll to get a bead - analogous to not needing to use Corr ranges in LOS. If you can't see the other side, you'd need to draw a bead, which can take quite some time, but you can use GPS coordinates or maps as your source data, or draw a bead on someone or something you know is at the far end.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T20:57:20-07:00","id":972319,"title":"","content":"This sort of silliness is why I would just as soon roll the connections business into regular Correspondence, have it be an alternate way of establishing said connection, and limit the character to using whichever makes sense for their Focus. Leaves us all with fewer headaches.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T12:29:06-07:00","id":972645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966506-data-sphere-question?p=972319#post972319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This sort of silliness is why I would just as soon roll the connections business into regular Correspondence, have it be an alternate way of establishing said connection, and limit the character to using whichever makes sense for their Focus. Leaves us all with fewer headaches.</div> </div> </div> </div>Current Data as Correspondence re-skinned with some extra and ill-explained fiddly bits is kinda a wash. <br /> <br /> &quot;Data&quot; a Sphere that's name has even less to do with what it affects than &quot;Entropy&quot; (which actually DOES address entropy among a host of other things).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}